{"type":"message","id":"aadc113a","parentId":"96b1a502","timestamp":"2026-07-28T12:53:30.915Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The database exists but has no tables. Let me look for the feed card system. Based on the memory entry, it looks like feed jobs might be in a different system. Let me check the cron message format again: `[cron:86c9ae68-4a25-4272-a484-1df297ead282 feed-drain-coinography-20260728-125140]`. This looks like a UUID followed by a timestamp.\n\nActually, looking at SOUL.md more carefully, I see that FEED_DRAIN mode uses `--feed-job-id` parameter. The UUID `86c9ae68-4a25-4272-a484-1df297ead282` might be the actual feed job ID. Let me check if it expects a string or integer:\n\n<｜DSML｜function_calls"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_17ebb143ab874641a495d916","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"source /tmp/coinography-run-env.sh\n# Let me check the actual script to see what format it expects\necho \"Checking build_picker_input.py source...\"\npython3 -c \"\nimport sys\nsys.path.insert(0, '/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-orchestrator/skills/pipeline')\ntry:\n    import build_picker_input\n    print('Module loaded')\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(f'Error: {e}')\n\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"bedrock-mantle","model":"deepseek.v3.2","usage":{"input":18318,"output":306,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":18624,"cost":{"input":0.01172352,"output":0.00058446,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.01230798}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1785243204856,"responseId":"chatcmpl-969c32d8-bc6e-49d6-b800-da76a9a47848"}}
