{"type":"message","id":"94451645","parentId":"97945bc9","timestamp":"2026-07-28T12:53:36.553Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Let me try a different approach. Since this is a cron-triggered FEED_DRAIN, maybe I should check if there's a specific way to handle this. Let me look for feed card callbacks in EDITORIAL_FEEDBACK.md:\n\n<｜DSML｜function_calls"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_9a35fa8f8dbb499791a029f2","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-orchestrator/EDITORIAL_FEEDBACK.md"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"bedrock-mantle","model":"deepseek.v3.2","usage":{"input":18654,"output":119,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":18773,"cost":{"input":0.01193856,"output":0.00022729,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.01216585}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1785243211072,"responseId":"chatcmpl-42e3b91a-ba00-48f7-8136-1c3d09192e8f"}}
{"type":"message","id":"00548c4b","parentId":"94451645","timestamp":"2026-07-28T12:53:36.690Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_9a35fa8f8dbb499791a029f2","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# EDITORIAL_FEEDBACK.md — News Card Editorial Feedback\n\nHandles Telegram feedback on news cards sent after pipeline execution.\n**DO NOT** start the pipeline or spawn subagents when handling editorial feedback.\n\n---\n\n## When This Applies\n\n| Incoming Callback / Text | Action |\n|--------------------------|--------|\n| `oc_r:`, `oc_ri:`, `oc_ri_menu:`, `RATE 8`, `IMAGE 7` | Rate article or feature image |\n| `oc_draft:`, `oc_draft_yes:`, `oc_draft_no:`, `DRAFT` | Unpublish flow (switch status to draft) |\n| `oc_publish:`, `oc_pub_a:`, `oc_pub_y:`, `oc_pub_n:`, `PUBLISH` | Publish flow (in-card author picker: Toby/Ahmed/Golan) |\n| `oc_edit:`, `oc_edit_apply:`, `oc_edit_cancel:`, `EDIT` | Edit flow (download `.md` -> upload edited `.md` -> apply) |\n| `oc_go:`, `oc_feed_refresh:` | Feed card callbacks (handled by `feed-tap-claimer` or handler) |\n| Document reply (`.md` file) | Apply edited Markdown file to WordPress post |\n\n---\n\n## Execution Protocol\n\nRun `handle_card_feedback.py` immediately in `bash`:\n\n```bash\npython3 ~/.openclaw/workspace-orchestrator/skills/pipeline/handle_card_feedback.py \\\n  --payload \"<callback data if present>\" \\\n  --message-text \"<user text if present>\" \\\n  --chat-id \"<telegram chat id>\" \\\n  --user-id \"<telegram user id>\" \\\n  --username \"<telegram username if known>\" \\\n  --reply-to-message-id \"<replied-to message id if present>\" \\\n  --document-file-id \"<telegram file_id if document upload>\" \\\n  --document-name \"<original filename if document upload>\"\n```\n\n### Output Rules\n- **Silent Turn:** If the handler sent a Telegram reply directly, OR if stdout is `NO_REPLY`, **end your turn silently with NO output text**.\n- **Error Handling:** If the handler prints an explicit error line (not `NO_REPLY`), output that line.\n\n---\n\n## Callback Mechanics Summary\n\n### 1. Feed-Card Taps (`oc_go:`, `oc_feed_refresh:`)\n- Intercepted by `feed-tap-claimer` plugin in-process zero-LLM.\n- Fallback in orchestrator: Run `handle_card_feedback.py`.\n- `oc_go:` enqueues job in `feed_jobs` DB table and edits card. End turn (drainer runs pipeline asynchronously).\n\n### 2. PUBLISH Flow\n- `oc_publish:{run_id}` $\\rightarrow$ Shows author buttons (Toby: 3, Ahmed: 17, Golan: 8).\n- `oc_pub_a:{run_id}:{author_id}` $\\rightarrow$ Publishes post live on WordPress immediately with chosen author byline.\n\n### 3. EDIT Flow\n- User replies `EDIT` $\\rightarrow$ Handler sends `article-{run_id}.md`.\n- User uploads updated `.md` file $\\rightarrow$ Handler compares diff (+N / −M lines) and presents **Apply** / **Cancel** buttons.\n- **CRITICAL:** Pass `--document-file-id` of the user's uploaded document from message metadata.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1785243216690}}
{"type":"message","id":"409d6a89","parentId":"00548c4b","timestamp":"2026-07-28T12:53:47.133Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I see. So feed-card taps like `oc_go:` are handled by `feed-tap-claimer` plugin. This cron event might be the result of such a tap being processed. Let me check if there's a feed jobs table somewhere else. Actually, looking at the error message from earlier: `PICKER_INPUT_ERROR: feed_job_not_found: id=125140 (job reclaimed/cleared, or wrong id passed)`. This suggests the feed job ID is numeric.\n\nLet me look for recent feed jobs in a different location:\n\n<｜DSML｜function_calls"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_ea213888a623409a8757e3e6","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"source /tmp/coinography-run-env.sh\necho \"Looking for feed job data...\"\nfind ~/.openclaw -name \"*feed*\" -type f 2>/dev/null | grep -i job | head -10"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"bedrock-mantle","model":"deepseek.v3.2","usage":{"input":18970,"output":204,"cacheRead":576,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":19750,"cost":{"input":0.0121408,"output":0.00038963999999999996,"cacheRead":0.00009216,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.012622600000000001}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1785243216691,"responseId":"chatcmpl-a5054617-eb80-4578-b29c-00228bbe5d8a"}}
