{"type":"message","id":"d8ad8b63","parentId":"db809bfa","timestamp":"2026-07-28T12:54:14.313Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"So I need one of those sources. Since this is a FEED_DRAIN, I need to use --feed-job-id. Let me check if there's a way to get the feed job ID from the cron system. Looking back at the memory entry, I see `Feed Card: f-coinography-20260623-125300`. This suggests feed jobs might be tracked differently.\n\nActually, wait. Looking at the cron message again: `[cron:86c9ae68-4a25-4272-a484-1df297ead282 feed-drain-coinography-20260728-125140]`. This looks like it's logging a cron execution. The format suggests `cron:<uuid> <task-name>`. So `feed-drain-coinography-20260728-125140` is the task name.\n\nMaybe I'm overthinking this. Let me check if there's a specific way FEED_DRAIN entries are supposed to work. Looking at SOUL.md again:\n\n**Entry Routing Table:**\n```\nFEED_DRAIN (drainer cron) | classify-only | OFF | Feed drain entry (use --feed-job-id)\n```\n\nSo I need to use `--feed-job-id`. But what should the ID be? Looking at the memory entry again:\n```\n**Job ID:** 13  \n**Feed Card:** f-coinography-20260623-125300\n```\n\nThe job ID was 13. So maybe I need to find what the current job ID is. Let me check if there's a way to query pending feed jobs:\n\n<｜DSML｜function_calls"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_216cfcc1d7864531bf213777","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"source /tmp/coinography-run-env.sh\necho \"Trying to find feed job ID...\"\n# Let me check if there's a command to list feed jobs\npython3 ~/.openclaw/workspace-orchestrator/skills/pipeline/mark_feed_job.py --help 2>&1"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"bedrock-mantle","model":"deepseek.v3.2","usage":{"input":20325,"output":437,"cacheRead":576,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":21338,"cost":{"input":0.013008,"output":0.0008346699999999999,"cacheRead":0.00009216,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.01393483}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1785243246491,