{"type":"message","id":"86cc5e8b","parentId":"4a634d10","timestamp":"2026-07-28T12:54:27.163Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The feed_jobs.db exists but has no tables. This is strange. Let me check if tables should be created dynamically. Maybe I need to initialize the database. Let me look at how feed jobs are created in the first place.\n\nLooking back at EDITORIAL_FEEDBACK.md, I see:\n- `oc_go:` enqueues job in `feed_jobs` DB table and edits card.\n\nSo when someone taps \"GO\" on a feed card, it creates a feed job. But if the database has no tables, maybe something is wrong with the setup.\n\nLet me check if there's an initialization script:\n\n<｜DSML｜function_calls"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_1b3015679b934a2bb12918b5","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"find ~/.openclaw -name \"*.sql\" -o -name \"*schema*\" -o -name \"*init*\" | grep -i feed | head -10"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"bedrock-mantle","model":"deepseek.v3.2","usage":{"input":21973,"output":206,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":22179,"cost":{"input":0.01406272,"output":0.00039346,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.01445618}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1785243261931,"responseId":"chatcmpl-f75c3454-d708-4f50-8856-59e49cd6b319"}}
